    "title": "Taking the fear out of public speaking - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Shawna Currie ,\n40 minutes ago Many people dread public speaking, but a local professor is changing that.\nPublic Speaking Mark Ward with TAMUV talks about his textbook and approach to teaching public speaking\nTexas A&M University–Victoria communication professor Dr. Mark Ward is gaining national recognition for his innovative approach to teaching the skill. His textbook, Introduction to Public Speaking: An Inductive Approach , recently received the 2025 Distinguished Textbook Award from the National Communication Association.\nInstead of having students deliver full speeches right away, Ward’s method focuses on building confidence step by step - starting with short, simple exercises. He says the approach helps reduce anxiety and make public speaking more approachable, especially for first-generation college students.\nWard said he hopes his work helps students develop communication skills that will benefit them both professionally and personally.\nGot a news tip or story idea? Email us at staff@crossroadstoday.com and include the best way to reach you. See breaking news call the 25 News Now newsroom 361-576-0026.\n​COPYRIGHT 2025 BY CROSSROADS TODAY. ALL RIGHTS RESERVED. THIS MATERIAL MAY NOT BE PUBLISHED, BROADCAST, REWRITTEN OR REDISTRIBUTED.",
